              "units": 1.0
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "audit_criteria",
          "type": "checklist",
          "label": "Loss prevention audit criteria",
          "items": [
            "Scope and reviewer authority are documented",
            "Key, seal, door, alarm, and restricted-area checks are complete",
            "High-value and transaction interfaces are represented",
            "Device status avoids exposing security credentials",
            "Observations, reports, and assumptions are separated",
            "Evidence access is limited and custody is recorded",
            "Personal information is proportionate to the event",
            "Response stayed within non-confrontation limits",
            "Exceptions have owner, escalation, and due point",
            "Outcome language avoids unsupported accusation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "audit_boundary",
          "type": "notice",
          "label": "Audit conclusion boundary",
          "guidance": "This form does not authorize surveillance expansion, profiling, confrontation, pursuit, search, detention, accusation, or access to restricted evidence. Record objective facts and minimum necessary personal information. Keep footage, credentials, and sensitive evidence in approved restricted systems. Follow applicable privacy, security, legal-request, and emergency policy and route decisions to the authorized professional reviewer."
        }
      ]
    },
